{# One wrapper, one dispatch.

   Every field is rendered and then concealed rather than omitted, so the form
   degrades to a long scrollable page when scripts fail instead of to a blank
   one ([10.6a]). The wrapper carries the field's name and required state as
   data attributes because the stepper toggles both as conditions change, and
   it must not have to re-derive which control belongs to which field.

   `cols` is how many fields the author put on a row, not how many columns one
   field spans: `cols: 2` is the half-width treatment that puts First Name
   beside Last Name, and `cols: 1` is a field with the row to itself. The page
   grid is two columns wide, so the two map to one cell and to both.

   Both class names are written out in full. The span used to be interpolated
   as `sm:col-span-{{ field.cols }}`, which Tailwind's scanner cannot see --
   it reads source text, not rendered output -- so the rule was never compiled
   and every field collapsed into a single cell whatever the markup claimed. A
   class name that is built at render time is a class name that does not
   exist.

   `runtime_class` and `runtime_id` are the form author's own hooks, set in the
   builder for the CSS they write in `settings.injectCss`. They land here, on
   the wrapper, for two reasons: it is the one element every field type has --
   a heading and an alert have no control to carry them -- and the ids further
   down are load-bearing. `intake-<name>` is what the label points at, what an
   error is described by and what a choice group names itself from, so an
   authored id must be able to sit beside that wiring and never displace it.

   The authored class is appended to the layout class rather than replacing it:
   naming a class must not cost a field its grid cell. Tailwind never sees
   these values either, which is correct -- they are the author's selectors,
   defined in the author's own CSS, not utilities for this build to compile. #}
<div class="{{ field.cols > 1 ? 'sm:col-span-1' : 'sm:col-span-2' }}{% if field.runtime_class %} {{ field.runtime_class }}{% endif %}"
     {%- if field.runtime_id %} id="{{ field.runtime_id }}"{% endif %}
     data-intake-field="{{ field.name }}"
     data-intake-type="{{ field.type }}"
     data-intake-required="{{ field.required ? '1' : '0' }}"
     data-intake-hidden="{{ field.hidden ? '1' : '0' }}"
     {% if field.conditions_json %}data-intake-conditions="{{ field.conditions_json }}"{% endif %}
     {% if field.hidden %}hidden{% endif %}>
  {% include 'partials/intake/' ~ field.template with { field: field } only %}
</div>
